dratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-2)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]-(-2)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-2)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410199 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410200 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410201 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410202 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410203 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1045 "Constrained Optimization of Quadratic Forms: Determining Where Extrema are Attained" 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1046 #edb/ref 17592186410202 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048933 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410164 1053 #uuid "f2727b60-7a6b-5f3a-a237-6a67bfb8139d" 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410165 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [17592186410165 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533592 17592186045417 true] [175921